Thanks for the update. I added the fix used by Dominick and tested the vari=
ous=0Afixes that are now okay. However (sorry) but one new bug has been int=
roduced=0Aand some others are still present:=0A=0A1) New bug - I've been us=
ing tunables to select the different levels of=0A=A0=A0 support between Tre=
sys and NSA compilers. Since this update, mapping=0A=A0=A0 inside tunables =
does not work (but only when using classpermissionset).=0A=A0=A0 The "tunab=
le-mapping-error.cil" module demos this error.=0A=0A2) classmapping only ta=
kes the first entry whether in a boolean or not. The=0A=A0=A0 "map-perm-err=
or.cil" module demos this error. The Tresys compiler has=0A=A0=A0 a differe=
nt problem - see text in "map-perm-error.cil".=0A=0A3) Fails to resolve nev=
erallow "*". The "neverallow-STAR.cil" module demos=0A=A0=A0 this error.=0A=
=0A4) Not sure if this is a bug or 'as designed', I tried using "in" in a=
=0A=A0=A0 booleanif statement but failed. The "in-boolean.cil" module demos=
=0A=A0=A0 this error.=0A=0AThese only apply to the Tresys compiler (as do 2=
, 3, & 4):=0A5) Does not expand all entries in a typeattribute for allow ru=
les within=0A=A0=A0 a boolean. The "ta-bool-error.cil" module demos this er=
ror.=0A=0A6) Neverallow fails when rule defined in a dontaudit rule. The NS=
A compiler=0A=A0=A0 and checkpolicy do not generate an error.=A0 The "never=
allow-error.cil" =0A=A0=A0 module demos this error.=0A=0AThe attached "cil-=
base.cil" supplies the user, role etc. requirements=0A=0AFinally I know the=
 NSA version resolves constraints okay now, but the output=0Ais reversed in=
 Tresys. The "mlsconstrain-diff.cil" shows the difference but=0Ain the end =
they resolve to the same. I have not tried complex constraints.=0A=0AHope a=
ll this helps=0ARichard
